stream
Order4th July 2023(Throug h Video Conferencing)
1. The complainants abovenamed have filed the present 16appllcations for non-compliance of the various MahaRERA Ordersissued in the above-mentioned Complaints (hereinafter referred toas the said complaints), by the respondent'
2. In the said complaints filed by the complainants, the respondentwas directed to refund of the amounts paid by the complainantsto the respondent along with the interest at the rate of 10.5olop.a. from the date of receipt till they are refunded. Therespondent was also directed to pay cost of Rs. 20,000/- to eachof the complainants.
3. On the said non-compliance application, the hearing was heldthrough video conferencing as per the MahaRERA Circular no.27l2O2O and MahaRERA Order No. t5/2020.
4. During the hearing, the complainants submitted that therespondent has failed to comply with the orders issued by thel"lahaRERA authority and has not refunded the amounts to thecomplainants along with the applicable interest at 10.50/o p.a. tothe complainants as per the said orders. The complainantstherefore sought the issuance of recovery warrants against therespondent under section 40(1) of RERA.
5. The respondent did not appear for the hearing even though thenotice of hearing was duly served upon it.Page 4 of 5

endstream
